Healer is one of my favorite classes as well.  If you get a good one
going, their Quest Artifact is one of the best weapons in the game. 
They are difficult in the first few levels, though.
 
My suggestion if you find an altar is to use stone-to-flesh on any
boulders on the level.  Usually there's 2-3 boulders on a level and
that gives you plenty of meat.  If you kill something away from the
altar that's too heavy to lift, you can always eat it instead.  You
can always head down to Sokoban as well if you're having problems
finding food, because a lot of food is generated there.  Remember, the
higher level your char is, the harder the monsters generated, so the
earlier you walk down to Sokoban the easier it will be.  Some people
go to Sokoban even before they enter the Gnomish Mines.
 
If you ever piss off your God, he/she will only be mollified by
corpses of some of the harder monsters that only appear in the deeper
levels (starting around dlvl 10 or so) so if it's a high-level altar
you might as well just try to move on and get some food.

